====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q1420}}A wheeled vehicle that moves independently, with at least three wheels, powered mechanically, steered by a driver and mostly for personal [[transportation]].
#: {{syn|en|auto|motorcar|vehicle|automobile|q4=US|motor|q5=Britain, colloquial|carriage|q6=obsolete|Thesaurus:automobile}}
#: {{ux|en|She drove her '''car''' to the mall.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Jordan Houston; Darnell Carlton; Paul Beauregard; Premro Smith; Marlon Goodwin; David Brown; Willie Hutchinson|passage=I'm a stunt; ride in the '''car''' with some bump in the trunk.|url=https://genius.com/Three-6-mafia-stay-fly-lyrics|title=Stay Fly|publisher=Sony BMG|year=2005|album=Most Known Unknown|artist=Three 6 Mafia (featuring Young Buck, 8 Ball, and MJG)}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=w:Edwin Black|title=Internal Combustion| chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL4103950W| passage=If successful, Edison and Ford—in 1914—would move society away from the ever more expensive and then universally known killing hazards of gasoline '''cars''':&nbsp;[&hellip;]&thinsp;.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[wheeled]] [[vehicle]], drawn by a [[horse]] or other animal.
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Edward 2|year=1622|text=It shall suffice me to enioy your loue,<br>Which whiles I haue, I thinke my selfe as great,<br>As ''Caesar'' riding in the Romaine streete,<br>With captiue kings at his triumphant '''Carre'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Antony and Cleopatra|IV|8|text=He has deserved it [armour], were it carbuncled<br>Like holy Phoebus’ '''car'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Eddison Worm|19|The Red Foliot sate in his '''car''' of polished ebony, drawn by six black horses with flowing manes and tails; before him went his musicians, pipers and minstrels doing their craft, and behind him fifty spearmen, weighed down with armour and ponderous shields that covered them from chin to toe.}}
## {{lb|en|dated}} A [[cart]].
## {{lb|en|dated}} A [[chariot]].
## {{lb|en|UK|Birmingham|obsolete}} A four-wheeled [[cab]], as opposed to a (two-wheeled) [[Hansom cab]].
# Any vehicle designed to run on rails, especially an unpowered one [[tow#Verb|towed]] by being connected to others.
## {{lb|en|rail transport|chiefly|North America}} An unpowered unit in a [[railroad]] train, used to hold either passengers or cargo.
##: {{syn|en|railcar|wagon|carriage}}
##: {{ux|en|The conductor coupled the '''cars''' to the locomotive.}}
## A similar vehicle used in special contexts, such as mines, quarries, and mills.<!--often construed as coordinate rather than hyponymous-->
##: {{hypo|en|mill car|mine car|quarry car|skip car}}
## {{lb|en|rail transport}} an individual vehicle, powered or unpowered, in a [[multiple unit]].
##: {{ux|en|The 11:10 to London was operated by a 4-'''car''' diesel multiple unit.}}
## {{senseid|en|passenger-carrying unit in a subway or elevated train, whether powered or not}}{{lb|en|rail transport}} A passenger-carrying unit in a [[subway]] or elevated train, whether powered or not.
##: {{ux|en|From the frontmost '''car''' of the subway, he filmed the progress through the tunnel.}}
## A [[rough]] [[unit]] of quantity approximating the amount which would fill a [[railroad]] car.
##: {{syn|en|carload|wagonload}}
##: {{ux|en|We ordered five hundred '''cars''' of gypsum.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1907|author=Texas Agricultural; Mechanical College System|journal=Bulletin| volume=93-117| page=5| passage=This market reports only one or two '''cars''' per day, selling by the hundred weight, and at a price a little lower than that of Indian corn.}}
# The moving, load-carrying component of an [[elevator]] or other [[cable]]-drawn transport mechanism.
#: {{ux|en|Fix the '''car''' of the express elevator - the door is sticking.}}
# The passenger-carrying portion of certain [[amusement park]] rides, such as [[Ferris wheel]]s.
#: {{syn|en|carriage}}
#: {{ux|en|The most exciting part of riding a Ferris wheel is when your '''car''' goes over the top.}}
# The part of an [[airship]], such as a [[balloon]] or [[dirigible]], which houses the passengers and control apparatus.
#: {{syn|en|gondola|basket|q2=balloons only}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1850|author=[[w:John Wise (balloonist)|John Wise]]|title=[http://books.google.com/books?id=sfYOAAAAYAAJ A System of Aeronautics]|page=152
|passage=Everything being apparently in readiness now, I stepped into the '''car''' of the balloon, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage="What about a''' car?'''" "The''' car '''will be my next care. I have already planned how it is to be made and attached. Meanwhile I will simply show you how capable my apparatus is of supporting the weight of each of us."}}
# {{lb|en|sailing}} A sliding fitting that runs along a track.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=Ken Textor|title=The New Book of Sail Trim|page=201|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=2JIbS0c1XPwC|isbn=0924486813| passage=On boats 25 feet or more, it is best to mount a mast '''car''' and track on the front of the mast so you can adjust the height of the pole above the deck}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|US|informal}} The aggregate of desirable characteristics of a car.
#: {{ux|en|Buy now! You can get more '''car''' for your money.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} A floating perforated box for living fish.
# {{lb|en|US|prison slang}} A [[clique]] or [[gang]].
# {{lb|en|internet}} {{deliberate misspelling of|en|cat}}{{rfv-sense|en}}

